-# @deepseek-ai/dsh-skill-settings
-
-English | [中文](README.zh.md)
-
-Harness-local per-skill invocation modes. The plugin stores `skill-settings.modes` in the active Harness settings provider and registers one policy with `ctx.skills`. It never modifies a discovered `SKILL.md`.
-
-`enabled` permits model and user invocation, `manual-only` permits only a user `/name` invocation, and `disabled` permits neither. A missing entry inherits `enabled`. The registry intersects every mode with the provider-authored frontmatter policy, so a local setting cannot re-enable an entry whose author disabled model or user invocation.
-
-The base bundle mounts this plugin beside `dsh-skill`; without a settings provider the policy remains enabled and contributes no durable state.
-
-## Model Experience
-
-`manual-only` and `disabled` entries disappear from the model catalog. `disabled` entries also fail the user-explicit invocation path. The setting adds no prompt text or tool schema.
-
-#### KV Cache effect
-
-Changing a model-visible mode can cause `dsh-tool-skill` to publish its normal replacement skill catalog, which changes the retained session suffix. No mode adds a separate prompt section.
-
-## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
-
-- **One Host-wide mode map** — settings apply to every session served by the Harness instance; project- or preset-specific mode maps are not supported.
-- **Discoverable entries only** — a mode for a missing skill remains stored and takes effect if that name is discovered later.
